@startuml
title Feature 002 - Durable Automatic Writeback and Recovery
participant "End Command" as End
database SQLite as DB
participant Worker as W
participant "Owner Runtime Credentials" as V
participant "Original Google Sheet" as S
End -> DB : transaction: ended + results + unique job + receipt
DB --> End : COMMIT
End -> W : wake (page may close)
W -> DB : claim pending job, original owner + sheetId
W -> V : credentials for job owner only
alt no original owner authorization
  V --> W : unavailable
  W -> DB : pending / GOOGLE_AUTH_REQUIRED
  note right of W : Owner reauthorization wakes verification.\nOther account tokens are never substituted.
else authorized
  loop each winning question or complete question group
    W -> S : read original sheetId structure and target values
    alt original owner authorization unavailable
      W -> DB : pending / GOOGLE_AUTH_REQUIRED\nno budget consumed, no scheduled retry
    else transient read failure
      W -> DB : persist read failure count + due time\nafter 4 transient failures: pending, paused
    else structure changed or mixed/unexpected values
      W -> DB : entire question conflict
    else all expected
      W -> DB : verified, no new write
    else all baseline and structure matches
      alt write budget remains in current cycle
      W -> DB : one transaction: writing + attempt + write count increment\nmax 3, retain retry cycle across restart
      DB --> W : committed
      W -> S : single batch updateCells\nall subitems, stringValue, value-only field mask
      alt timeout / response lost / process crash
        W -> DB : pending if process alive
        note right of DB : On restart durable writing becomes pending.\nReadback first; never blind resend.
      else response received
        W -> S : readback original sheetId
        S --> W : current values
        W -> DB : verified only if all expected\notherwise pending/conflict with safe reason
      end
      else 3 write attempts already consumed
        W -> DB : failed / AUTO_RETRY_EXHAUSTED\nonly after baseline confirmed
      end
    end
  end
end
note over W,DB
Google calls never run inside SQLite transactions.
Persistence failure stops dispatch; never false verified.
Repeated end or history view does not create another job.
No winners: zero-item verified job, no write API call.
Write retry delays: 2s / 4s, precheck before each write.
Read failure delays: 1s / 2s / 4s, then pending pause.
Unknown outcome never becomes failed solely from retry limit.
Only explicit owner retry opens a new durable cycle.
Same retry requestId never opens another cycle.
end note
@enduml
